# Round 17, L §5.16 A random number of items: "read by a range that ends at the draw (sum(x[m, s] for s in 1 .. n[m]
# step 1) ...; a draw of a dist with no unit is a num, so the range states its step, §5.11)"; L §5.11 "a range of
# quantities without step is refused (LOAD-DOMAIN)"; L §8.3 LOAD-DOMAIN `range of quantities <a> .. <b> has no step`.
# L5_16_random_items_run is this model with `step 1`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "s"
index slots = int 1..3
input trials: int
input cost[k in slots]: num
input n: dist
def total: num = sum(cost[k] for k in 1 .. n)

ask q: mean(total) paths 20 seed 1

version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  trials = 5
  cost[*] = 2
  n = binomial(trials, 0.99)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN range of quantities 1 .. n has no step ...
